# Option B (docs/VRAM_1MB_OPTIONS.md): card VRAM lives on the HPS DDR3
# channel instead of the SDRAM window. The THREE macros move TOGETHER (a
# tripwire in MacIIvi.sv enforces the pairing): with card VRAM on DDR3,
# sdram.v's window-release mechanism buys nothing and is unvalidated on
# hardware (the v2.2 wedge — docs/resume_2026-08-07_vram_1mb.md), and its
# video port is dead weight (ALMs + muxes on the clk_64 arbitration), so
# B builds compile both out and run the pre-release controller shape.
# Comment all three out to fall back to Option A.
# BISECT (2026-08-09, branch misc-fixes): owner reports game crashes with
# the DDR VRAM build — this build takes ONLY the DDR change out and puts
# Card VRAM shape (2026-08-10 rollback): 300KB hot BRAM + cold tail to the
# presented 512KB in the SDRAM window — the months-proven port-B scanout,
# restored after BOTH streamed backends (DDR3 and the SDRAM burst port)
# misbehaved on hardware. The streamed experiment (24bpp Millions, the
# window-release mechanism, mdc_scan_fetch/mdc_vram_ddr) lives in this
# branch's history from 8c60798 through eeb3393 if it is ever revisited.
# ^ bisect-retreat shape (2026-08-09, misc-fixes): card scans out of 300KB
# hot BRAM (MDC_VRAM_WORDS=153600 in MacIIvi.sv), so the SDRAM video port
# is dead weight again — compiled out along with the window-release. DDR
# stays off. The cold tail to 1MB still rides the SDRAM cpu slot.
set_global_assignment -name VERILOG_FILE rtl/floppy_track_encoder.v
set_global_assignment -name VERILOG_FILE rtl/floppy.v
set_global_assignment -name SYSTEMVERILOG_FILE rtl/ps2_kbd.sv
set_global_assignment -name SYSTEMVERILOG_FILE rtl/adb.sv
set_global_assignment -name VERILOG_FILE rtl/ps2_mouse.v
set_global_assignment -name VERILOG_FILE rtl/scc.v
set_global_assignment -name VERILOG_FILE rtl/uart/txuart.v
set_global_assignment -name VERILOG_FILE rtl/uart/rxuart.v
set_global_assignment -name VERILOG_FILE rtl/swim.v
